From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Santiago Hormazabal <santiagohssl@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] net: dsa: qca8k: clear the SGMII PLL bits on the RB953GS

EN_PLL, EN_RX and EN_TX in SGMII_CTRL are set at reset on the AR8327,
and the driver only ever sets them.

On the MikroTik RB953GS, port 6 is wired to an SFP cage, and with these
bits set the SerDes never links up, neither with a copper SFP module in
SGMII mode nor with a DAC in 1000BASE-X mode. The SGMII_CTRL value used
for AR8327 SGMII designs on ar71xx (0xc70167d0) has them cleared too.

Clear them on this board.

Signed-off-by: Santiago Hormazabal <santiagohssl@gmail.com>
---
--- a/drivers/net/dsa/qca/qca8k-8xxx.c
+++ b/drivers/net/dsa/qca/qca8k-8xxx.c
@@ -1559,6 +1559,10 @@ static int qca8k_pcs_config(struct phyli
 	if (priv->ports_config.sgmii_enable_pll)
 		val |= QCA8K_SGMII_EN_PLL | QCA8K_SGMII_EN_RX |
 		       QCA8K_SGMII_EN_TX;
+	else if (of_machine_is_compatible("mikrotik,routerboard-953gs-5hnt"))
+		/* The SerDes does not link up with these set */
+		val &= ~(QCA8K_SGMII_EN_PLL | QCA8K_SGMII_EN_RX |
+			 QCA8K_SGMII_EN_TX);
 
 	if (dsa_is_cpu_port(priv->ds, port)) {
 		/* CPU port, we're talking to the CPU MAC, be a PHY */
